# The PDA writing zone's key strip (report 041) in the terminal (CLI), as the mockup shows it: Keys opens the strip
# between the app area and the soft buttons (the terminal leaves its row free, as for the on-screen keyboard), Ctrl tapped
# is armed (lit) for the next key; a "c" written in the letters box then sends Ctrl+C (the fake shell echoes ^C and a new
# prompt) and Ctrl goes off; a pound sign (the extended prefix, then an l) reaches the terminal as UTF-8 text (its own
# font draws it). Keys again closes the strip. Goldens at both sizes.
title zone strip
sizes 480x640 480x800
profile pda
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
launch CLI
ptyout "user@pda:~$ "
wait 300
zonekey Keys
expect_zone strip open
zonekey Ctrl
shot zone_strip_ctrl
stroke letters 117,55 110,46 102,38 92,32 81,30 69,31 59,34 49,42 44,55 41,67 40,78 41,89 45,101 50,111 58,120 68,127 80,130 91,127 101,120 110,110 115,103
shot zone_strip_ctrl_c
stroke letters 60,30 145,115
stroke letters 60,30 60,130 121,130
ptylog zone_strip_pty
shot zone_strip_pound
zonekey Keys
expect_zone strip closed
shot zone_strip_closed
